#. ~ Description of "12 gauge buckshot"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A 12 gauge shotgun shell, filled with 9 pellets of 00 buck.  A very common "
"and versatile round, they're useful for both self defense and for hunting.  "
"The spread of the shot doesn't just increase your chances to have a "
"projectile hit, it also causes a much larger wound, greatly increasing "
"lethality.  It does struggle with range, and against body armor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "12 gauge beanbag"
msgid_plural "12 gauge beanbags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "12 gauge beanbag"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A beanbag round for shotguns.  Designated 'less-lethal' and intended to "
"disable, but remember that 'less-lethal' does not mean 'non-lethal'."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "12 gauge birdshot"
msgid_plural "12 gauge birdshot"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "12 gauge birdshot"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"Weak shotgun ammunition, filled with tiny pellets and a low powder charge.  "
"Used often for shooting clays or birds, they're a very common commercial "
"round.  Their effectiveness against human targets are quite limited outside "
"of very close ranges, serving more to hurt than kill."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "12 gauge dragon's breath"
msgid_plural "12 gauge dragon's breath"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "12 gauge dragon's breath"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A shotgun shell filled with magnesium pellets or shards, used mostly as a "
"distress flare or pyrotechnics tool.  When the round is fired, high-"
"temperature sparks and flames shoot out of the barrel.  While looking very "
"impressive, they present more of a fire hazard than an effective tool for "
"lighting up hostiles."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "12 gauge flechette"
msgid_plural "12 gauge flechettes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "12 gauge flechette"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A shotgun shell filled with tiny steel darts.  While looking quite dangerous,"
" their actual effectiveness is questionable.  Despite being finned, they have"
" a tendency to tumble mid-air, leading to greater spread and reduced damage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "12 gauge explosive slug"
msgid_plural "12 gauge explosive slugs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "12 gauge explosive slug"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A shotgun shell shooting a small explosive.  Banned in several states.  While"
" an explosive from a shotgun sounds impressive, its practical applications "
"are limited at best.  The loss in mass in order to accommodate an explosive "
"give it much less impact force compared to traditional ammunition.  The "
"relatively small size of the slug can only accommodate a limited amount of "
"explosives, resulting in a fairly underwhelming explosion.  These traits make"
" it a utility tool for damaging barriers and disrupting other explosive "
"devices, rather than something for anti-personnel use."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "12 gauge buckshot, scrap loaded"
msgid_plural "12 gauge buckshot, scrap loaded"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "12 gauge buckshot, scrap loaded"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A shotgun shell filled with whatever scrap metal was lying around.  More "
"damaging than birdshot, but fairly inaccurate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "12 gauge, black powder, scrap loaded"
msgid_plural "12 gauge, black powder, scrap loaded"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "12 gauge, black powder, scrap loaded"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A shotgun shell filled with black gunpowder and whatever scrap metal was "
"lying around.  The logical conclusion of ammunition bootlegging.  It'll kill "
"zombies just fine, but your gun will suffer for it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "12 gauge slug"
msgid_plural "12 gauge slugs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "12 gauge slug"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A 12 gauge slug.  Unlike birdshot or buckshot, slugs are a single large "
"projectile fired from a shotgun.  They're mostly used for hunting bigger "
"game, or for longer range shots where typical buck may spread out more.  Not "
"as lethal as buckshot in certain ranges, but much more accurate and with a "
"longer range, and is more effective against armor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid "wax slug"
msgid_plural "wax slugs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "wax slug"
#: data/json/items/ammo/shot.json
msgid ""
"A round of 12 gauge birdshot that has had the crimp opened, and wax poured "
"into the shot to mimic the performance of a proper slug."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sling-ready Molotov cocktail"
#: data/json/items/ammo/sling-ready_grenade.json
msgid ""
"A bottle of flammable liquid with a long fuse inserted, ready to be used in a"
" staff sling with a modified cradle.  To throw this item without a sling, use"
" it light the fuse.  You will, of course, need a lighter or matches in your "
"inventory to do this.  After lighting it, throw it to cause fires."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sling-ready grenade"
#: data/json/items/ammo/sling-ready_grenade.json
msgid ""
"A military-grade fragmentary hand grenade, modified with a retaining fuse for"
" use in a staff sling with a modified cradle.  To throw this item without a "
"sling, use it to snap the fuse and activate the grenade.  You will then have "
"five seconds before it explodes; throwing it would be a good idea."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sling-ready small homemade grenade"
#: data/json/items/ammo/sling-ready_grenade.json
msgid ""
"An improvised explosive device cobbled together from spare parts and modified"
" with a retaining fuse for use in a staff sling.  To throw this item without "
"a sling, use it to snap the fuse and activate the grenade.  You will then "
"have 5 seconds before it explodes; throwing it would be a good idea."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sling-ready homemade grenade"
#: data/json/items/ammo/sling-ready_grenade.json
msgid ""
"An improvised explosive device cobbled together from spare parts and modified"
" with a retaining fuse for use in a staff sling with a modified cradle.  To "
"throw this item without a sling, use it to snap the fuse and activate the "
"grenade.  You will then have 5 seconds before it explodes; throwing it would "
"be a good idea."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sling-ready military explosive small homemade grenade"
#: data/json/items/ammo/sling-ready_grenade.json
msgid ""
"An improvised explosive device cobbled together from parts and modified with "
"a retaining fuse for use in a staff sling.  To throw this item without a "
"sling, use it to snap the fuse and activate the grenade.  You will then have "
"some amount of time before it explodes; throwing it would be a good idea."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sling-ready military explosive homemade grenade"
#: data/json/items/ammo/sling-ready_grenade.json
msgid ""
"An improvised explosive device cobbled together from parts and modified with "
"a retaining fuse for use in a staff sling with a modified cradle.  To throw "
"this item without a sling, use it to snap the fuse and activate the grenade."
"  You will then have some amount of time before it explodes; throwing it "
"would be a good idea."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "oxyacetylene"
#: data/json/items/ammo/weldgas.json
msgid ""
"Pressurized, dangerous acetylene gas.  Can be used for welding or cutting "
"with a torch."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "welding rod"
#: data/json/items/ammo/weldgas.json
msgid ""
"A length of coated welding electrode - a 3 mm thick steel rod coated in a "
"special flux.  During the welding process, the hot metal of the electrode "
"fills the seam, jointing parts together while the flux protects the surface "
"of the seam from atmospheric gases and rapid cooling.  Required for arc "
"welding."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "aluminum welding rod"
#: data/json/items/ammo/weldgas.json
msgid ""
"A length of coated welding electrode - a 3.2 mm thick aluminum rod coated in "
"a special protective flux.  Required for arc welding aluminum alloys."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "welding wire"
#: data/json/items/ammo/weldgas.json
msgid "A length of 0.8 mm steel wire for MAG welding."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "aluminum welding wire"
#: data/json/items/ammo/weldgas.json
msgid "A length of 0.9 mm aluminum wire for MIG welding."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "brazing rod"
#: data/json/items/ammo/weldgas.json
msgid "A length of 3.2 mm flux-coated bronze rod, for brazing steel."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "aluminum brazing rod"
#: data/json/items/ammo/weldgas.json
msgid ""
"A length of 3.2 mm aluminum rod, for brazing aluminum alloys.  Also suitable "
"for TIG welding."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "portable gasoline generator"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_generators.json
msgid ""
"Small, portable generator, one that people buy for a camp.  It just needs to "
"be plugged in, fueled up, and then turned on."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "diesel generator"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_generators.json
msgid ""
"Big and powerful generator, used for street works.  It just needs to be "
"plugged in, fueled up, and then turned on.  Has little wheels to make it "
"easier to move."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid "household fridge"
msgid_plural "household fridges"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "household fridge"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected household refrigerator.  General choice to store some "
"perishables for an average family.  Activate to deploy and connect to your "
"electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "minifridge"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected minifridge, similar to ones in some luxury limousines.  "
"Activate to deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "food truck fridge"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A heavy and bulky fridge with little wheels for easier transportation.  Has a"
" bunch of sections and separators, which allow it to be installed in a "
"vehicle with relative assurance that any items inside will stay put.  "
"Activate to deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "single glass door fridge"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected commercial refrigerator with a transparent glass door, "
"designed to show off any cold drinks and similar goods in a grocery store "
"while still keeping them cool.  Activate to deploy and connect to your "
"electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "double glass door fridge"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected commercial refrigerator with two transparent glass doors, "
"designed to show off any cold drinks and similar goods in a grocery store "
"while still keeping them cool.  Activate to deploy and connect to your "
"electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "heavy-duty fridge"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected commercial refrigerator, used in many professional kitchens.  "
"Activate to deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "display fridge"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A big glass chamber, designed to display different food in a multiple rows, "
"while cooling it at the same time.  While you might not need to actually "
"display any of your food, it cools the food as good as any another fridge.  "
"Activate to deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid "household freezer"
msgid_plural "household freezers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "household freezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected household freezer.  Great choice if you need to freeze some "
"discount meat.  Activate to deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "minifreezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A compact version of an upright freezer, designed as a mobile solution for "
"freezing food.  Activate to deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chest minifreezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A compact version of a chest freezer, designed as a mobile solution for "
"freezing food, but it's pretty tricky to pull anything out from the bottom.  "
"Perfect choice to put in your closet and forget for a year.  Activate to "
"deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "food truck freezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A heavy and bulky freezer with little wheels for easier transportation.  Has "
"a bunch of sections and separators, which allow it to be installed in a "
"vehicle with relative assurance that any items inside will stay put.  "
"Activate to deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chest freezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A hefty chest freezer, designed to store plenty of perishables for a "
"minuscule amount of power.  Activate to deploy and connect to your electric "
"grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "heavy-duty freezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty upright freezer.  Big as a closet, heavy as a tank, can probably"
" fit enough meat to feed a little colony for a week, but consumes power like "
"no other.  Activate to deploy and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "glass door freezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected commercial freezer with a glass door, used to present "
"different frozen goods.  Activate to deploy and connect to your electric "
"grid."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "display freezer"
#: data/json/items/appliances/appliances_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A disconnected commercial chest freezer with a glass lid.  Activate to deploy"
" and connect to your electric grid."
msgstr ""

